nlsh (1.3ppa1) noble; urgency=low

  * Renamed package from osh to nlsh: "osh" clashed with an unrelated
    PyPI package (Jack Orenstein's Object SHell). The command is now nlsh.
  * Safety gate: QA verdicts are matched to commands by number; a command
    without a verdict counts as WARN instead of running ungated.
  * Every command is confirmed before it runs while safety is on; only
    PASS defaults to yes, and end of input means no. The safety setting
    is honoured and -a forces the prompt.
  * LLM output is stripped of ANSI sequences and hidden characters before
    display; commands containing hidden characters are rejected.
  * install.sh removes legacy osh installs only if they contain osh.py
    and only after asking.

 -- Raul Kivi <raul.kivi@proton.me>  Mon, 12 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000

osh (1.2ppa1) noble; urgency=low

  * Add llama.cpp llama-server backend support (api="llama_cpp",
    llama_cpp_endpoint), selectable via --init and install.sh.
  * Sanitize llama.cpp model names/log fields against terminal escape
    and log-injection sequences; validate response content type.

 -- Raul Kivi <raul.kivi@proton.me>  Mon, 07 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000

osh (1.1ppa1) noble; urgency=low

  * Fix retry-after-failed-execution bypassing the availability/QA safety
    checks on the regenerated command.
  * Add missing python3-ollama runtime dependency.
  * Fix setuptools build-backend declaration.
  * Bump minimum ollama dependency to 0.6.2.

